# ==============================================================================
# This file has been split in two.
# ==============================================================================
# There is no longer a single .env driving every environment — the development
# and production stacks now have their own templates, because roughly a dozen
# of these values genuinely have to differ (secrets, public origin, cookie
# security, rate limits, worker counts) and a shared file quietly hid that.
#
#   development →  cp .env.development.example .env.development  &&  make dev
#   production  →  cp .env.production.example  .env.production   &&  make prod
#
# See ENVIRONMENTS.md for what each variable does, and for the short list that
# Next.js bakes into the client bundle at build time — those need a rebuild
# when changed, not a restart.
#
# Running the backend on its own in a virtualenv, outside Docker? That path
# still uses Backend/.env.example.
# ==============================================================================
